.TH RK-HDMI-STREAMER 1 "2026" "rk-hdmi-streamer 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rk-hdmi-streamer \- low-latency Rockchip MPP/RGA HDMI capture & multi-stream RTSP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rk-hdmi-streamer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rk-hdmi-streamer
captures HDMI video from V4L2 UVC capture devices and audio from ALSA, encodes H.264/H.265 using Rockchip MPP hardware (with optional RGA DMA-BUF conversion and scaling), and outputs either:
.IP \(bu 2
a direct single-thread \fBepoll\fR RTSP/TCP server supporting multiple simultaneous on-demand output streams (including downscaled, lower-FPS, and audio-only endpoints) sharing one capture source;
.IP \(bu 2
an RTSP publisher (\fB\-o rtsp://...\fR); or
.IP \(bu 2
a raw Annex-B H.264/H.265 elementary stream to a file or \fBstdout\fR (\fB\-o \-\fR) for Unix piping.
.PP
All long flags accept both \fB\-\-option value\fR and \fB\-\-option=value\fR.
Diagnostic output goes to \fBstderr\fR so \fBstdout\fR remains clean for \fB\-o \-\fR and \fB\-\-print\-config\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General & Unix Composability
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read INI configuration before CLI flags. Use \fB\-\fR to read from \fBstdin\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate the effective configuration and exit (\fB0\fR if valid, \fB2\fR on error).
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Write the effective normalized INI configuration to \fBstdout\fR and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress periodic statistics and startup diagnostics on \fBstderr\fR (errors still print).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose RTSP session tracing (alias for \fB\-\-rtsp\-debug\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-stats\-interval " N"
Statistics interval in seconds (\fB0\fR disables periodic stats; default \fB5\fR).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and compiled feature flags (\fBrga\fR, \fBopus\fR, \fBlibyuv\fR, \fBneon\fR) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show option summary and exit.
.SS Capture Input
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " " \fIPATH\fR
V4L2 video capture node (prefer \fI/dev/v4l/by-id/...\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-stream\-profile " NAME"
Capture pipeline preset: \fBmjpeg\fR (MJPEG DMA-BUF \-> MPP JPEG), \fBrga\fR (YUYV DMA-BUF \-> RGA NV12), or \fByuyv-libyuv\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-input\-format " FMT"
Raw V4L2 pixel format: \fBmjpeg\fR or \fByuyv\fR/\fByuy2\fR (default \fBmjpeg\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-yuyv\-converter " CONV"
YUYV\-to\-NV12 converter: \fBrga\fR or \fBlibyuv\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-rga\-library " PATH"
Explicit path to \fIlibrga.so\fR (also respects \fBRGA_LIBRARY\fR env var).
.TP
.BR \-\-v4l2\-dmabuf ", " \-\-no\-v4l2\-dmabuf
Enable or disable zero-copy V4L2 DMA-BUF capture into MPP/DRM buffers.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " " \fIW\fBx\fIH\fR
Set width and height together (e.g. \fB1920x1080\fR, \fB1280x720\fR). Also available individually via \fB\-\-width\fR and \fB\-\-height\fR.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-fps " " \fIN\fR
Capture or stream frame rate (default \fB50\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-video\-range " RANGE"
Color range metadata: \fBlimited\fR, \fBfull\fR, or \fBunspecified\fR.
.SS Video Encoder (Rockchip MPP)
.TP
.BR \-\-video ", " \-\-no\-video
Enable or disable video track. Setting \fBvideo=false\fR on an RTSP stream creates an audio-only endpoint that never opens V4L2, MPP, or RGA.
.TP
.BI \-\-video\-codec " CODEC"
\fBh264\fR or \fBh265\fR/\fBhevc\fR (default \fBh264\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-rc\-mode " MODE"
Rate control mode: \fBcbr\fR or \fBvbr\fR (recommended for lower network/CPU load).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bitrate " " \fIRATE\fR
Target bitrate in bit/s. Accepts human suffixes \fBk\fR/\fBK\fR, \fBm\fR/\fBM\fR, \fBg\fR/\fBG\fR (e.g. \fB15M\fR, \fB2.5M\fR, \fB2500k\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-gop " N"
Key-frame interval in frames (default \fB50\fR).
.SS Audio Capture (ALSA)
.TP
.BR \-\-audio ", " \-\-no\-audio
Enable or disable audio capture and RTP audio track.
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-device " ID"
ALSA capture device (default \fBhw:CARD=Video,DEV=0\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-codec " CODEC"
\fBopus\fR (48 kHz stereo) or \fBl16\fR (uncompressed 16-bit PCM).
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-gain " N"
Fixed-point Q16 PCM gain multiplier before encoding (default \fB1.0\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-frame\-ms " MS"
Audio packet duration: \fB2.5\fR, \fB5\fR, \fB10\fR, \fB20\fR, \fB40\fR, or \fB60\fR ms (default \fB20\fR).
.SS Output & Multi-Stream RTSP Server
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Write raw Annex-B video to \fIPATH\fR (\fB\-\fR for \fBstdout\fR) or publish to an \fBrtsp://\fR URL.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen\-rtsp " " \fIADDR\fR
Start direct RTSP/TCP server listening on \fIADDR\fR (e.g. \fB:8554\fR, \fB0.0.0.0:8554\fR, \fB[::1]:8554\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-rtsp\-path " PATH"
Default stream path (default \fB/capture\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-rtsp\-stream " SPEC"
Add an on-demand simultaneous output stream using comma-separated \fBkey=value\fR pairs (alias: \fB\-\-rtsp\-profile\fR). Supported keys include \fBname\fR, \fBpath\fR, \fBvideo\fR, \fBaudio\fR, \fBcodec\fR, \fBsize\fR/\fBwidth\fR/\fBheight\fR, \fBfps\fR, \fBbitrate\fR, \fBrc-mode\fR, \fBgop\fR, and \fBsend-timeout-ms\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-rtsp\-send\-timeout\-ms " MS"
Maximum stalled TCP write duration before closing a slow client (default \fB2000\fR; use \fB8000\fR\-\fB12000\fR for mobile/car links).
.TP
.BI \-\-rtsp\-idle\-grace\-ms " MS"
Keep MPP/RGA resources warm after the last client disconnects while pausing V4L2 capture (default \fB3000\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-rtp\-payload " BYTES"
Maximum RTP payload size per packet (default \fB1400\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-clients " N"
Maximum concurrent RTSP clients (default \fB3\fR, max \fB16\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " N"
Stop cleanly after \fIN\fR encoded frames (\fB0\fR runs forever).
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
INI files use \fB[capture]\fR (alias \fB[main]\fR) for the shared hardware input and default stream, followed by any number of \fB[stream.\fINAME\fB]\fR (alias \fB[profile.\fINAME\fB]\fR) sections. CLI flags override INI values.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown and clean release of V4L2, MPP, RGA, ALSA, and sockets.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Immediately print current capture and RTSP statistics to \fBstderr\fR.
.TP
.B SIGUSR2
Force an immediate IDR keyframe on all active video encoders.
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Ignored so broken downstream pipes (\fB\-o \-\fR) exit cleanly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, \fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR, or valid \fB\-\-check\-config\fR / \fB\-\-print\-config\fR.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (device, MPP/RGA, ALSA, I/O, or network failure).
.TP
.B 2
CLI usage or configuration validation error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Pipe 1080p50 raw H.264 directly to \fBffplay\fR over SSH:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ssh board 'rk-hdmi-streamer -s 1920x1080 -r 50 -b 8M --rc-mode=vbr --no-audio -q -o -' | ffplay -f h264 -
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quick ad-hoc multi-stream RTSP server (LAN + car + audio-only):
.PP
.RS
.nf
rk-hdmi-streamer --stream-profile=rga -s 1920x1080 -r 50 -b 15M --rc-mode=vbr \\
  --audio-codec=opus -l :8554 --rtsp-path=/hq --max-clients=5 \\
  --rtsp-stream path=/coche,size=1280x720,fps=25,codec=h265,bitrate=2M,rc-mode=vbr,gop=25,send-timeout-ms=10000 \\
  --rtsp-stream path=/audio,video=false,audio=true,send-timeout-ms=12000
.fi
.RE
.PP
Validate a config from \fBstdin\fR and trigger live stats / IDR on a running daemon:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rk-hdmi-streamer -c - --check-config < /etc/rk-hdmi-streamer.conf
pkill -USR1 rk-hdmi-streamer   # dump live stats
pkill -USR2 rk-hdmi-streamer   # force instant IDR keyframe
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR v4l2-ctl (1),
.BR arecord (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR pidstat (1)
